{
  "_comment": [
    "Venue list. This is how a headline gets a city and a tier, and it is the",
    "single biggest lever on accuracy - a venue named in a headline is a much",
    "harder fact than any phrase guess.",
    "",
    "Each entry:",
    "  name     the house, written the way the site should display it",
    "  city     New York | Chicago",
    "  tier     Broadway | Off-Broadway | Off-Off-Broadway | Chicago major | Chicago storefront",
    "  match    lowercase substrings to look for in the headline and summary",
    "  requires (optional) one of these must ALSO appear, for ambiguous names",
    "  excludes (optional) if any of these appear, this entry does not match",
    "",
    "Ambiguity is the thing to watch. Chicago and New York share house names:",
    "Nederlander, Palace and Auditorium exist in both cities. Those entries",
    "carry requires/excludes so a Chicago story is never filed as Broadway.",
    "Single-word surnames that are also common words (Booth, Hayes, Golden,",
    "Palace) only match with 'theatre' or 'theater' attached.",
    "",
    "Headline text naming no venue at all falls back to the plain words",
    "'Broadway' and 'Off-Broadway', which the ingest treats as New York. A",
    "story with neither goes to the review bucket rather than onto the page."
  ],

  "fallbacks": {
    "_comment": "Used only when no venue matched. Order matters: first hit wins.",
    "rules": [
      { "match": ["off-off-broadway"], "city": "New York", "tier": "Off-Off-Broadway" },
      { "match": ["off-broadway", "off broadway"], "city": "New York", "tier": "Off-Broadway" },
      { "match": ["broadway in chicago", "chicago theatre", "chicago theater", "in chicago"], "city": "Chicago", "tier": "Chicago major" },
      { "match": ["broadway"], "city": "New York", "tier": "Broadway" }
    ]
  },

